replaces everything except for the prefix (if any) of self . if path has a prefix but no root, it replaces self . if self has a verbatim prefix (e.g. \\?\C:\windows )
and path is not empty, the new path is normalized: all references
to . and .. are removed. Consider using Path::join if you need a new PathBuf instead of
using this function on a cloned PathBuf . § Examples Pushing a relative path extends the existing path: use std::path::PathBuf; let mut path = PathBuf::from( "/tmp" );
path.push( "file.bk" ); assert_eq! (path, PathBuf::from( "/tmp/file.bk" )); Pushing an absolute path replaces the existing path: use std::path::PathBuf; let mut path = PathBuf::from( "/tmp" );
